- ### Choosing an engine
+ ### Elegir un motor

- The default engine is the JVM's own. Its backtracking can take exponential time on a
- pathological pattern and input. This is
- [catastrophic backtracking](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ReDoS), which turns a regular
- expression applied to untrusted input into a denial of service. `re2` is an automaton engine
- written in Scala, which avoids it. The price is the constructs which an automaton cannot
- express:
+ El motor predeterminado es el de la propia JVM. Su retroceso puede tardar un tiempo exponencial
+ con un patrón y una entrada patológicos. Esto es el
+ [retroceso catastrófico](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ReDoS), que convierte una expresión regular
+ aplicada a una entrada no fiable en una denegación de servicio. `re2` es un motor de autómatas
+ escrito en Scala, que lo evita. El precio son las construcciones que un autómata no puede
+ expresar:

= express:
=
- ```tabular
+ ```tabular

- column  Engine
+ column  Motor

- column  Given
+ column  Given

- column  Time
- column  Constructs
- row  the JVM's  `regexBackends.javaBaseRegex`, the default  exponential, at worst  every construct of its syntax
- row  re2  `regexBackends.re2`  linear in the length of the input  all but backreferences and lookaround
+ column  Tiempo
+ column  Construcciones
+ row  el de la JVM  `regexBackends.javaBaseRegex`, el predeterminado  exponencial, en el peor caso  todas las construcciones de su sintaxis
+ row  re2  `regexBackends.re2`  lineal en la longitud de la entrada  todas salvo las retrorreferencias y los lookaround

= row  re2  `regexBackends.re2`  linear in the length of the input  all but backreferences and lookaround
- ```
+ ```

- The engine is a [given], so a program chooses it with an import, and the patterns are unchanged:
+ El motor es un [given], así que un programa lo elige con una importación, y los patrones no
+ cambian:

= The engine is a [given], so a program chooses it with an import, and the patterns are unchanged:
=
- ```scala fuel
+ ```scala fuel

= The engine is a [given], so a program chooses it with an import, and the patterns are unchanged:
=
= ```scala fuel
- run
+ run

= The engine is a [given], so a program chooses it with an import, and the patterns are unchanged:
=
= ```scala fuel
= run
